# SQL's `'it''s'`: DS0117 with a fix to `\'`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where customerId != 'it''s'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..43
  PIPELINE@0..42
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..42
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..42
        NAME_REF@21..31
          IDENT@21..31 "customerId"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
        NEQ@32..34 "!="
        WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
        LITERAL@35..42
          STRING@35..39 "'it'"
          STRING@39..42 "'s'"
  WHITESPACE@42..43 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `''` does not put a quote in a string
  --> query:1:39
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where customerId != 'it''s'
  |                                       ^^ this ends the string and starts another
  |
  = help: escape the quote with a backslash: `'it\'s'`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where customerId != 'it\'s'
which parses without errors
